WEBVTT

00:00.810 --> 00:04.990
Elizabeth starts out 5
miles away from school

00:04.990 --> 00:08.880
and walks away from school
at 3 miles per hour.

00:08.880 --> 00:10.330
So she's already 5 miles away.

00:10.330 --> 00:12.000
And she's going to
walk even further

00:12.000 --> 00:14.570
away at 3 miles per hour.

00:14.570 --> 00:17.680
The table below shows how
far some other students

00:17.680 --> 00:20.660
are from school
at various times.

00:20.660 --> 00:25.270
Each person is moving at a
constant speed starting at time

00:25.270 --> 00:27.780
is equal to 0.

00:27.780 --> 00:31.020
Which students started
out farther from school

00:31.020 --> 00:31.930
than Elizabeth?

00:31.930 --> 00:33.939
Select all that apply.

00:33.939 --> 00:35.480
So essentially, we
need to figure out

00:35.480 --> 00:38.060
where these students
were at time equals 0.

00:38.060 --> 00:41.940
So we know where they
were at time 1, 2, and 3.

00:41.940 --> 00:43.840
And so let's think
about their rate

00:43.840 --> 00:46.660
towards or away from school.

00:46.660 --> 00:50.590
And remember, this is
distance from school.

00:50.590 --> 00:54.680
As we increase-- as we
go from hour 1 to hour 2,

00:54.680 --> 00:57.420
Gordon gets 2 miles closer.

00:57.420 --> 01:01.410
So his distance to
school is decreasing.

01:01.410 --> 01:03.916
So where was he
at time equals 0?

01:03.916 --> 01:06.290
I'll put time equals 0 up here
because I don't have any--

01:06.290 --> 01:07.270
actually, I'll
put it right here.

01:07.270 --> 01:09.080
I'll try to squeeze
it into the chart.

01:09.080 --> 01:11.990
So where was he
at time equals 0?

01:11.990 --> 01:15.640
Well, he would have
been 2 miles further.

01:15.640 --> 01:18.370
So he would have
been 6 miles away.

01:18.370 --> 01:19.870
Notice that it's consistent.

01:19.870 --> 01:22.270
In the first hour,
he would have gotten

01:22.270 --> 01:24.145
2 miles closer to school.

01:24.145 --> 01:25.520
Then the next
hour, he would have

01:25.520 --> 01:27.200
gotten 2 miles even closer.

01:27.200 --> 01:29.720
And then the third hour, he
actually gets 2 miles closer.

01:29.720 --> 01:31.490
And he actually gets to school.

01:31.490 --> 01:36.860
So Gordon started out 6
miles away at t equals 0.

01:36.860 --> 01:39.970
So Gordon did start out farther
from school than Elizabeth.

01:39.970 --> 01:41.620
So we can circle Gordon.

01:41.620 --> 01:43.200
He meets the conditions.

01:43.200 --> 01:45.730
Now let's think about Giovanni.

01:45.730 --> 01:49.840
So at time 1, he's 5
miles away from school.

01:49.840 --> 01:54.150
Then at 1 hour,
he's 5 miles away.

01:54.150 --> 01:56.890
After 2 hours,
he's 6 miles away.

01:56.890 --> 01:59.350
So he's getting
further from school.

01:59.350 --> 02:01.410
So this is a plus 1.

02:01.410 --> 02:04.130
And then after another
hour, he is 7 miles away.

02:04.130 --> 02:07.790
So every hour that goes
by, he's a mile further.

02:07.790 --> 02:11.110
He's going 1 mile an
hour away from school.

02:11.110 --> 02:14.640
So where was he at time equal 0?

02:14.640 --> 02:17.110
Well, he would have been
a mile closer to school

02:17.110 --> 02:18.750
relative to time equal 1.

02:18.750 --> 02:21.470
So he would have
been 4 miles away.

02:21.470 --> 02:23.880
So he did not start out
farther than Elizabeth,

02:23.880 --> 02:26.540
who started out 5 miles away.

02:26.540 --> 02:28.350
Now let's look at Hannah.

02:28.350 --> 02:32.880
Hannah, at every time, is
just exactly 5 miles away

02:32.880 --> 02:34.070
from school.

02:34.070 --> 02:35.840
So she's napping or something.

02:35.840 --> 02:39.050
She is not actually moving.

02:39.050 --> 02:43.570
She started out napping at
exactly the same distance

02:43.570 --> 02:47.075
as Elizabeth, but she did not
start out farther from school

02:47.075 --> 02:47.700
than Elizabeth.

02:47.700 --> 02:51.470
So Hannah does not
meet the criteria.

02:51.470 --> 02:53.050
Now let's look at Alberto.

02:53.050 --> 02:58.370
At time equals 1, he
is 9 miles from school.

02:58.370 --> 03:04.580
And then after 1 hour, he
gets a mile and 1/2 further

03:04.580 --> 03:05.870
from school.

03:05.870 --> 03:10.540
After another hour, he gets
a mile and 1/2 even further.

03:10.540 --> 03:12.796
So where was he
at time equals 0?

03:12.796 --> 03:15.170
Well, he would have been a
mile and 1/2 closer to school.

03:15.170 --> 03:20.680
So 9 minus 1.5 is-- he would
have been 7 and 1/2 miles away.

03:20.680 --> 03:24.200
So even though he is
going away from-- well,

03:24.200 --> 03:28.810
he definitely started further
from school than Elizabeth.

03:28.810 --> 03:30.540
Elizabeth started
out 5 miles away.

03:30.540 --> 03:33.200
Alberto started off
7 and 1/2 miles away

03:33.200 --> 03:35.820
and is going even further
and further and further.

03:35.820 --> 03:38.070
So the two students that
start out farther from school

03:38.070 --> 03:42.350
than Elizabeth are
Gordon and Alberto.
